  "problem": "Express $S=11+22+33+⋯+242+253$ using sigma notation.\n\n|  | {{field-1}} |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,\\,\\,\\,S=$ | $\\sum $ | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n|  | $\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{}^{n=1}$ |  |  | $\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$ |",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that the terms of the corresponding sequence\n\n$$\n11,\\,22,\\,33,\\,…,\\,242,\\,253.\n$$\n\nare multiples of $11.$ Since $253÷11=23,$ there are $23$ terms in total. \n\nTherefore, the $n$th term of the sequence has the form\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=11n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ ranges from $n=1$ to $n=23.$ Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =11(1)=11 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =11(2)=22 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =11(3)=33 \\\\  & \\,\\,⋮ \\\\ {a}_{22} & =11(22)=242 \\\\ {a}_{23} & =11(23)=253\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nS=11+22+33+⋯+242+253={\\sum }_{n=1}^{23}11n.\n$$",
